41 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 243 0 R
/E (Structural & Functional Role: The insular cortex is a structurally heterogeneous brain region involved in interoception, salience processing, and the integration of sensory, emotional, and bodily information. These functions support awareness of internal states and responses to environmental demands.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
42 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 244 0 R
/E (Developmental Maturation: Childhood and adolescence are characterized by ongoing cortical maturation. Examining insular cortical thickness during this period can help characterize age-related structural variation in a region that supports multiple cognitive and socioemotional processes.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
43 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 245 0 R
/E (Individual Differences: Brain maturation varies across individuals, brain regions, and potentially hemispheres and sex. Characterizing age-related and sex-based variation in bilateral insular thickness can help clarify patterns of structural variability in youth, providing a foundation for future studies of typical and atypical neurodevelopment.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
