100 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 254 0 R
/E (Descriptive Patterns: Mean cortical thickness was slightly greater in the right than the left insula. This descriptive difference provides context for the bilateral analyses but does not establish a statistically significant hemispheric difference.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [63]
>>
endobj
101 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 255 0 R
/E (Age-Related Variation: Older age was associated with lower cortical thickness in both hemispheres, indicating a consistent pattern of insular thinning across the 8-16 year age range. Age explained approximately 19-26% of the variance in the respective regression models, with a stronger association observed for the right insula.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [64]
>>
endobj
102 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 256 0 R
/E (Sex-Based Differences: No significant sex-based differences in age-adjusted cortical thickness were observed in either hemisphere. Within this sample, the results therefore provide no evidence of differences in mean insular thickness between male and female youth after accounting for age.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [65]
>>
endobj
